# No eol conversion, ever: the handshake tag digests shipped files as RAW BYTES
# (`map::content_digest` → `net::protocol::protocol_id`, ADR-0018). Git for Windows
# defaults core.autocrlf=true, and a CRLF-rewritten level.json inside a release zip
# mints a protocol id the server cannot decrypt (v0.5.0 Windows clients, 2026-08-16).
* -text

*.blend filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.glb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.dae filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Terrain: the game's surface texture library, one folder per pack holding its KTX2 maps
# (assets/terrain/<pack>/<pack>_{diff|col,nor_gl,arm}.ktx2, built by scripts/encode-terrain-ktx2.sh).
# `**/` matches zero or more directories, so a pack added without touching this file is still
# LFS-tracked. The png/jpg lines stay for any non-pack image dropped in here.
assets/terrain/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/terrain/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/terrain/**/*.ktx2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Maps: one folder per map (assets/maps/<id>/), holding its level.json manifest, the heightmap the
# manifest names, and derived/ for what we generate from it. Same extensions, same `**/` reach, so a
# map added without touching this file is LFS-tracked too.
assets/maps/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/maps/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
assets/maps/**/*.ktx2 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
